      "description": "Watch Dinamo Zagreb vs FC Thun highlights and goals from UEFA Champions League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on July 28, 2026. The atmosphere was electric as Dinamo Zagreb hosted FC Thun in a high-stakes UEFA Champions League encounter on July 28, 2026. This match proved to be a classic European night, filled with tactical shifts and an emotional roller-coaster that kept fans on the edge of their seats until the very last whistle. Early Shock for the Hosts The game began in nightmare fashion for the home side. Within just four minutes, FC Thun took a stunning lead through Brighton Labeau , who clinicaly finished a pass from Nassim Zoukit . Dinamo Zagreb struggled to find their rhythm, and their frustrations grew as Miha Zajc picked up an early booking. The situation turned from bad to worse in the 22nd minute when Marco Buerki doubled the visitors' lead, assisted by Fabio Fehr , leaving the Croatian champions staring at a mountain to climb. The Turning Point The momentum shifted dramatically in the 67th minute when goalscorer Marco Buerki was shown a straight red card. The decision sparked heavy protests from the FC Thun players, but the referee stood firm. With a man advantage, Dinamo Zagreb finally ignited. Dion Drena Beljo pulled one back in the 74th minute following a setup by Moris Valincic . The stadium erupted just five minutes later when substitute Lukas Kacavenda leveled the score, thanks to an assist from Fran Topic , forcing the contest into extra time. Extra-Time Drama and Victory The additional 30 minutes were a test of endurance. Dinamo Zagreb continued to pile on the pressure, and their persistence paid off in the 112th minute. Moris Valincic , turning from provider to scorer, netted the decisive goal after being played in by Josip Misic . Despite a late flurry of yellow cards for Arber Hoxha and Christopher Ibayi , and several tactical substitutions to kill the clock, Dinamo held on to secure a breathtaking 3-2 comeback victory."
